    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0391" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/1448</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-17T11:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 17, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your November 16, 1 p.m. Scholle when Chargé saw President Menocal at the time of
                    Department’s first inquiry and was informed <pb facs="0392" n="280"
                        xml:id="pg280"/> that suit against Rafael Manderley, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >et al.</hi>, was for taking part in revolution and is of the same character
                    as all suits against rebellious citizens. It has nothing whatever to do with
                    funds taken out of Cuba by Fernandez.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
